course: dictionary
lesson: 3385
title: Words from space
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An exoplanet is a planet that goes around a star other than our Sun. The word has two parts: «exo» is a prefix meaning outside, and «planet» you already know. Read the context to find the rest.
explain: «Most exoplanets have been found by the transit method: a star dims slightly when a planet passes in front of it.» The clue is dims. A star that dims gets a little less bright, so something must be passing in front of it. That is how astronomers spot many exoplanets.
explain: «The James Webb Space Telescope can study the air of some exoplanets.» Here the context tells you that exoplanets are real places far away, with air you can study. Ask yourself what word would fit: planets, so the sentence says some planets have air.
fact: Exoplanet means a planet that goes around a star other than the Sun.
fact: More than 6,000 exoplanets have been confirmed, and the number is still rising.
fact: Some exoplanets orbit two stars, like Kepler-16b, found in 2011.
fact: Scientists look for exoplanets in the «Goldilocks zone», where water could be liquid.
fact: No life has been found on any exoplanet so far.
exercise: «Most exoplanets have been found by the transit method.» What is an exoplanet? | A moon that goes around a planet | *A planet that goes around a star other than our Sun | A star that has burned out | A comet with a long tail
exercise: «No life has been found on any exoplanet so far.» What does this sentence tell you? | Scientists have found life on every exoplanet | Life lives only on the Sun | Exoplanets are all made of water | *Scientists have not yet found life on any exoplanet
exercise: «A star dims slightly when a planet passes in front of it.» What does dims mean? | Moves very fast across the sky | Grows much bigger | Turns into a planet | *Gets a little less bright
test: «The James Webb Space Telescope can study the air of some exoplanets.» What are exoplanets? | Stars that have burned out | Clouds of dust between the stars | Telescopes made in space | *Planets that go around stars other than our Sun
test: «Kepler-16b is a real world with two suns in its sky.» How many stars does Kepler-16b orbit? | Six thousand | *Two | One | Ten
exam: Scientists have found thousands of ___ going around other stars. Which word fits best? | Moons | Sunspots | *Exoplanets | Comets
